#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:239
msgid ""
"Emit ``#line`` directives in generated C-family source from TIR spans, "
"mapping generated statements back to their Python source lines. For example, "
"with the always-on ``-lineinfo`` for nvcc, PTX ``.loc`` entries point at the "
"Python source. Default: 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:244
msgid "The value is a level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:246
msgid "0 (or False): off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:247
msgid "1 (or True): one directive per statement that owns a TIR span."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:248
msgid ""
"2 or more: every emitted source line is re-anchored. Level 1 only anchors a "
"statement's first line, so a synthesized statement without a span keeps the "
"previous mapping (already advanced past its line), and a statement that "
"prints several source lines (for example a vectorized CUDA binary op) still "
"drifts inside the statement. Level 2 precedes every emitted line, including "
"closing braces, with a fresh directive: a span-less statement inherits the "
"nearest enclosing statement's span, then the function's span, then the last "
"statement's span, and a function whose PrimFunc has no span is mapped to the "
"``<tilelang-generated>`` pseudo-source instead of inheriting the previous "
"function's file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:259
msgid ""
"``TILELANG_EMIT_LINE_DIRECTIVES`` supplies the same default outside an "
"explicit pass config (for example in compile-only tools); it accepts the "
"same level values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/transform/pass_config/index.rst:268
